WhAt'S mEsSy ?
-*-*-*-*-*-*-*

 >Messy< is basically a small CLI tool that will write public EALL or
private messages from specified text files. It was intended to use with
schedule programs OR doors which don't create messages. If you want
a message to be written certain days/hours/minutes etc... I highly
recommend the use of Messy together with Cybercron schedule event program.
If you have a nice door which creates bulletins and you wish them as
public messages, you can use Messy as well. Just call it in your logoff
script or so.


WaRnInG..
*-*-*-*-*

 It sometimes happens that the first "character" in a textfile is a
clearscreen ansi code. Messy will simply remove it from the new message
in order to have the mail header displayed correctly at mail scanning.


hOw To LaUnCh It ?
*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-

 Messy will need the following parameters in order to work:
 
  * Path to target conference, with or without terminating "/".

  * Path+Filename of the text file to be inserted in the message base.

  * Source: name of the "user" who should have written the message.
    Usually the sysop's name :)

  * Subject: you know what should be here ;)
  
  * Eventually a DESTINATION user. If specified, the message will be private.


 If you wish to use spaces in the source, destination and subject fields,
then use quotes ("string").


 Example:
 -------

 MESSY BBS:amigaworld bbs:amigaworld/msgbase/verenaris.bull
   "Diogenes / Skid Row" "WEEKTOP RESULTS" John 


